  "id": "store/a-conversation-read-takes-50-messages-by-default-a-refused-one-included",
  "title": "get_conversation reads 50 messages when it names no limit, and from a cursor the first messages after it in index order, a refused message included, as a context holds the conversation",
  "rules": [
    "§14.1",
    "§7.5 rule 8"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-14.1-019"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: store/base.py get_conversation; roomkit-rs ConversationStore::get_conversation. The room holds 52 messages, the one at index 1 refused: a read with no limit holds 50 of them, and a read after a cursor holds the refused one, which the conversation a context holds keeps (§14.1, A timeline read serves what the room received). Not observed: which 50 messages a read without a cursor holds, which RK-14.1-019 does not name, and the read of a context itself (§10.1 step 3), which its hooks' scenarios observe.",
